1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,460
So, Leah, Josh, let's compare
the two possible sites.

2
00:00:03,999 --> 00:00:05,100
Start with Cliffside Bay.

3
00:00:05,345 --> 00:00:06,360
That's Site A.

4
00:00:07,029 --> 00:00:09,940
People assume the cliffs are clay
because of the colour of the water,

5
00:00:10,360 --> 00:00:11,740
but they're actually chalk.

6
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:15,880
And they're retreating fast,
about 30 centimetres a year.

7
00:00:16,425 --> 00:00:18,460
Marsh Point is roughly half that.

8
00:00:18,760 --> 00:00:21,280
Dr Patel, any dangers at Cliffside?

9
00:00:21,580 --> 00:00:25,720
Bits of the cliff come down regularly,
so rock falls are the main concern.

10
00:00:26,120 --> 00:00:27,440
How do you get down to the beach?

11
00:00:27,545 --> 00:00:32,100
There's no car park nearby, so you
walk down a coastal path from the clifftop.

12
00:00:32,245 --> 00:00:33,245
And the nearest town?

13
00:00:33,485 --> 00:00:35,820
Cliffside itself, about a mile inland.

14
00:00:36,615 --> 00:00:40,460
C-L-I-F-F-S-I-D-E.

15
00:00:40,680 --> 00:00:41,680
Now Marsh Point.

16
00:00:42,025 --> 00:00:43,120
Totally different.

17
00:00:43,565 --> 00:00:48,300
Sand dunes, no cliffs, eroding
at about 15 centimetres a year.

18
00:00:48,595 --> 00:00:49,595
Rock falls there too?

19
00:00:49,910 --> 00:00:51,360
There are no rocks to fall.

20
00:00:51,934 --> 00:00:53,940
The problem there is the sea coming in.

21
00:00:54,305 --> 00:00:58,220
At high tide, the lower areas are
underwater, so flooding is the risk.

22
00:00:58,520 --> 00:00:59,520
Access?

23
00:00:59,995 --> 00:01:00,995
Straightforward.

24
00:01:01,160 --> 00:01:03,800
You park in the car park
and walk onto the dunes.

25
00:01:04,259 --> 00:01:06,500
The nearest settlement
is Marsh Point Village.

26
00:01:06,879 --> 00:01:08,140
Which one is your main site?

27
00:01:08,390 --> 00:01:09,390
Marsh Point.

28
00:01:09,579 --> 00:01:13,480
But if the conditions are bad there,
we'll fall back on Cliffside, Site A.

29
00:01:13,839 --> 00:01:15,159
How will you organise the groups?

30
00:01:15,429 --> 00:01:19,500
We originally said five per group, but
four works better with the equipment.

31
00:01:19,825 --> 00:01:20,720
Equipment?

32
00:01:20,744 --> 00:01:24,020
A measuring tape and a
clinometer for the slope angles.

33
00:01:24,424 --> 00:01:27,340
We thought about GPS units,
but we don't really need them.

34
00:01:27,614 --> 00:01:29,893
Hard hats aren't
necessary at Marsh Point,

35
00:01:29,917 --> 00:01:32,372
but everyone must
wear high visibility vests.

36
00:01:32,729 --> 00:01:34,280
What about timing with the tide?

37
00:01:34,654 --> 00:01:38,540
We need it low, and on our date,
that's around 11 in the morning.

38
00:01:38,810 --> 00:01:39,720
And the journey?

39
00:01:39,744 --> 00:01:42,620
The coach takes about 45 minutes.

40
00:01:42,960 --> 00:01:46,520
I'll need your risk assessment by
Friday, not the day before the trip.

41
00:01:47,089 --> 00:01:48,496
Who will you check the weather with?

42
00:01:48,520 --> 00:01:49,520
The Coast Guard office.

43
00:01:49,784 --> 00:01:51,792
Their local information
is better than the

44
00:01:51,816 --> 00:01:54,172
national forecast, and
they cover the tides, too.

45
00:01:54,469 --> 00:01:55,669
How will you record your data?

46
00:01:55,924 --> 00:01:59,280
Paper sheets blow away, so
we'll use an app on a tablet.

47
00:01:59,679 --> 00:02:02,048
There'll be two of us
supervising, me and one

48
00:02:02,072 --> 00:02:05,240
colleague, and the report
has to be in within three weeks.

49
00:02:05,724 --> 00:02:09,639
Photographing the landscape is fine, but
no photographs of local residents, please.

50
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:11,100
How much is the coach?

51
00:02:11,845 --> 00:02:13,520
It's £8 each, return.

52
00:02:13,975 --> 00:02:15,200
The department pays the rest.

53
00:02:15,410 --> 00:02:18,120
Permission from the parish
council isn't enough, by the way.

54
00:02:18,530 --> 00:02:20,080
You need it from the district council.

55
00:02:20,890 --> 00:02:22,410
When will you make the final decision?

56
00:02:22,655 --> 00:02:23,820
We'll confirm by Monday.

57
00:02:24,220 --> 00:02:24,876
Good!

58
00:02:24,900 --> 00:02:26,380
This all sounds well-organised.

